    "fullStory": "Pure Prairie League's \"Amie\" reached #27 on the Billboard Hot 100. \"Amie\" is a song by the American country rock group Pure Prairie League.\n\nThe song initially appeared on the band's 1972 album, Bustin' Out.\n\nIt was subsequently released as a single in 1975, after it gained popularity as an album cut.\n\nThe song peaked at #27 on the Billboard Hot 100 and spent 13 weeks on the chart.\n\nChart story — peaked at #27 on the Hot 100."
